    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d215">

                <pb facs="0449" n="389" sameAs="frus:frus1944Quebec/pg389"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Roosevelt Papers: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the President</hi><anchor n="1" xml:id="d215-f1"
                    /></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1944-09-13">September 13, 1944</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Ambassador Winant’s telegram number 7511 sent midnight September 12th<anchor
                        n="2" xml:id="d215-f2"/> reports that the European Advisory Commission on
                    that date approved and signed, for submission to the three governments, the
                    protocol on zones of occupation in Germany (State Department’s <pb facs="0450"
                        n="390" xml:id="pg390"/> note: with British and American zones left in
                        blank<anchor n="3" xml:id="d215-f3"/>) and the administration of greater
                        Berlin.<anchor n="4" xml:id="d215-f4"/></p>
                <closer><signed>C[<hi rendition="#small-caps">ordell</hi>] H[<hi
                            rendition="#small-caps">ull</hi>]</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d215-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d215-f1-content">
                <p>Delivered to the White House Map Room; forwarded to Roosevelt at Quebec in
                    telegram No. <hi rendition="#small-caps"
                        >MR–out</hi>–397.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d215-f2" n="2" xml:id="d215-f2-content">
                <p>Not printed (740.00119 EAC/9–1244).</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d215-f3" n="3" xml:id="d215-f3-content">
                <p>This parenthetical note was in the telegram as sent.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d215-f4" n="4" xml:id="d215-f4-content">
                <p>The body of the protocol as signed on September 12, 1944, was identical with the
                    draft which Hull forwarded to Roosevelt on September 11, <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >ante</hi>, <ref target="#pg380">p. 380</ref>. For the formal text of the
                    signed protocol, see <ref target="frus1945Malta#pg_118"><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Foreign Relations</hi>, The Conferences at Malta and Yalta, 1945, p.
                        118</ref>; Department of State, Treaties and Other International Acts Series
                    No. 3071; Department of State, <hi rendition="#italic">United States Treaties
                        and Other International Agreements</hi>, vol. 5, part 2, p. 2079.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
